  "description": "Silver Birch in garden of 66 Combemartin Road on the north boundary of the property neighbouring 68 Combemartin Road. I propose to fully remove the tree and stump. We have a young family with a toddler and bought the property off an elderly couple. The garden needs to be a safe area for the toddler to play so we want a clear clean lawn. The tree drops leaves, twigs and debris on the lawn. It casts the garden into shadow. The lawn is poor quality and may be competing with the tree roots. Neighbours at 68 welcome the proposed removal as they too are troubled by falling debris. Neighbours at 21 Skeena Hill welcome the removal as their garden suffers from shade and they believe removing a surrounding tree can only help.",
